  "protocol": "Task 6: seeded synthetic calibration of the heuristic gait descriptor (gait_cue).\n\nProtocol, fixed before the run: a population of 40 synthetic walkers whose body and gait\nparameters are drawn uniformly from the ranges below; 4 sequences per walker, each with a\nrandom start phase, a within-walker cadence jitter of +/-5 percent, a random length of 32 to\n64 frames at 16 fps, and Gaussian keypoint noise. The gait vector is the first element of\ngait_cue(series). Genuine pairs: all pairs of sequences of the same walker. Impostor pairs:\nall pairs from different walkers. Distance: Euclidean between the two L2-normalised vectors.\nPrimary setting: noise 0.01, population seed 0. Secondary: noise 0.005 and 0.02, and\npopulation seeds 0 to 4 for the primary noise, to show spread. Skeleton geometry follows\ndemo/walkers.py of the face-free-reid product (coordinates are image-normalised units).\nRun: python3 -I t6_gait_calibration.py\n",
